nodecode-nexus is a rewrite of Neboy72's Neboy72/nexus-memory:

  https://github.com/Neboy72/nexus-memory
  commit 783488328eee1a9ae29ea6ae62bdb63be5dfade3
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Nebo (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's user-facing memory on the nexus Qdrant collection --
nexus_recall (with the point-in-time as_of), nexus_remember (category,
salience, confidence, access level, source), nexus_forget, the
nexus_guardrail_check that matches stored protection rules against a
destructive command's targets, and nexus_find_entities. The same payload
fields and the same collection name, so a cell and the original provider (or
any MCP-connected agent) read and write one memory. The prefetch of what the
store holds about the newest ask before each turn, and the write-back of a
finished turn, are carried; so is the access-level gate that fails closed on a
missing level, and the demotion of stored text that reads like an instruction.
The Python runtime of the original -- an embedded Qdrant client, a local
sentence-transformers stack, a private venv, a loopback embedding service and
the consolidation daemon -- is Common Lisp here: nlk:http speaks Qdrant's
REST API and an embeddings endpoint, one section declaration types the
settings, and five nlk:define-contract declarations type the tools'
arguments so the schema the model is shown and the body that runs are one
shape.

Left out: the parts of the original that are an engine rather than a Hermes
surface -- the knowledge-graph traversal and subgraph verbs (the edges ride
in each fact's payload; nexus_find_entities reads the entities without
walking them), the guardrail override audit record, the cost-aware routing
statistics, the SICA self-improvement cycle, the opt-in recall reranker, the
LLM fact extraction at session end (a cell takes no second model call, so a
finished turn is filed as the user's own sentence), the daily backups, the
watchdog self-check and status section, the update check, and the standalone
CLI, MCP server and dashboard, which are other front ends for the same
runtime.
